WEBVTT

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.114
Come in.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:21.153
Seven of Nine's shipwide
efficiency analysis.

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:23.155
Did we get a passing grade?

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:26.158
Barely. She wants to present it
to the senior staff.

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:27.158
Put her

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:28.159
on the schedule.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.320
We'll be passing

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:30.328
by a Class-T cluster

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:32.729
in the next couple of days...
gas giants,

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:33.731
radiogenic sources.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:34.824
I'm not sure it's worth

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:35.959
altering course.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.468
At the very least,

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.562
we should send the Delta Flyer
for a look,

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:42.665
and let's get a full range of
sensor scans as we get closer.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:48.504
We'll go to a level-3
analysis of the cluster.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:49.980
Tom, get the Flyer ready

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.608
and assemble an away team.

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.379
Harry, start continuous scans.

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:54.715
Kim to Seven of Nine.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:56.187
Proceed, Ensign.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:58.724
Any chance you can increase
radiogenic resolution

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.157
in the long-range sensors?

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.285
The Captain wants
to get a cleaner look

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:04.523
at that cluster
coming up off starboard.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.121
Acknowledged.

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:11.432
Take these specifications
to Lieutenant Torres.

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:12.801
Right away.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.717
Deck 11.

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.827
What's our Borg queen want now?

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:39.763
We need to route at least
another five terawatts

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:41.596
to the sensor array.

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:48.131
Deck 15.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:57.914
Hello.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.748
Sorry to interrupt.

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.416
I'm about to disprove

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:09.929
Schlezholt's theory
of multiple big bangs.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:11.588
Of course, I had to demolish

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.598
Wang's second postulate
to do it.

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:15.896
Power transfer requisition.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.336
You're standing in the way
of cosmological history.

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:22.602
The cosmos is
16 billion years old.

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:25.769
It can wait another few minutes.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.882
Schlezholt would thank you
for the reprieve.

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:44.449
Captain's Log, Stardate 53753.2.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.951
Long-range scans
of the T-cluster have indicated

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.954
a number
of tantalizing anomalies.

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.785
The away team should have
a field day.

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:53.951
Who knows?
I may even join them myself.

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:56.790
Billy...

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:58.455
Mm...

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:01.728
Billy, wake up.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.393
What do you want?

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:05.061
I need help.

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:06.070
Good night.

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:09.006
Billy, don't you dare
go back to sleep.

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:12.840
What's the problem?

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:14.607
I'm in trouble.

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:15.807
Go to sleep.

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:17.315
Help me first.

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:19.851
With what?

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:21.716
This level-3 sensor analysis.

00:05:21.788 --> 00:05:24.780
I've got four hours of subspace
infrared to interpret.

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:27.690
Long-range scans
on that cluster up ahead?

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:28.692
Yes.

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:29.693
It's too complicated

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:30.854
to do over the com.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.490
Either we meet in the Mess Hall,
or we wait until tomorrow.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:35.691
I don't want to get dressed,

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:36.928
and it can't wait
until tomorrow.

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:39.095
Your only options.

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:44.268
I've given operations
an efficiency rating of 76

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:46.209
out of a possible 100.

00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:47.769
Not exactly flying colors.

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:49.474
The crewmen you assign

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:50.948
to the night shift
are frequently left

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:52.882
with little to do once the
ship's course has been

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:53.884
locked in.

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.614
The devil finds work
for idle hands.

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:57.178
Religious metaphors

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:58.450
are irrelevant.

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:00.856
Perhaps you should consider
assigning them additional tasks.

00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:05.992
What's this I'm guilty of:
"Failure to utilize expertise"?

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:11.232
Crewman Mortimer Harren.

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:13.864
He has five advanced degrees

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:15.066
in theoretical cosmology,

00:06:15.141 --> 00:06:18.235
but you've assigned him
to the... Plasma Relay Room.

00:06:18.311 --> 00:06:20.142
His talents could be put
to better use.

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:21.305
B'Elanna?

00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:23.315
Believe me, I've tried.

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:24.577
When I give him
more responsibility,

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:25.742
he doesn't do the work.

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:28.286
Harren wants to be
down on Deck 15.

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:30.254
It gives him more
time to repostulate

00:06:30.323 --> 00:06:31.722
the origins of the universe.

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:33.190
As you can see,

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:35.386
security is functioning
at near-perfect efficiency.

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:36.792
However, Commander,

00:06:36.863 --> 00:06:39.855
if you arrange the phasers
in the weapons lockers

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:42.059
so that the smaller rifles
were in front, they could be

00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:44.035
more easily removed
in the event of an emergency.

00:06:44.103 --> 00:06:47.004
I'll look into it.

00:06:48.374 --> 00:06:50.774
Crewman William Telfer.

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:53.277
Billy. He certainly
ruined my score.

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:55.780
He visits the Sick Bay
almost once a week

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:57.281
complaining of illness.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:00.410
Invariably, you examine him
and find nothing wrong.

00:07:00.486 --> 00:07:02.351
Mr. Telfer is a hypochondriac.

00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:03.889
I'd treat him for it,

00:07:04.023 --> 00:07:05.888
but he's afraid of medication.

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:07.391
Have you tried counseling?

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:09.018
He's afraid of that, too.

00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:12.064
All I can do is scan him
and offer him reassurance.

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:14.122
Wasting your time
and medical resources.

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:16.300
What about Astrometrics?

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:17.893
Looks like you could use
some improvement

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:19.699
yourself, Seven.

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:22.366
You're correct, unfortunately.

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:27.406
Tal Celes,
Sensor Analyst, grade-3.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.471
Her work must be
constantly double-checked.

00:07:29.549 --> 00:07:31.915
She should be removed from
Astrometrics and reassigned

00:07:32.018 --> 00:07:34.543
elsewhere... perhaps
to Engineering.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:38.556
Forget it. I've got my own
problems to fix, remember?

00:07:38.624 --> 00:07:40.558
That'll be all, Seven.
Thank you.

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:43.962
Dismissed.

00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:50.600
Captain?

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:55.039
They've never been
on an away mission.

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:57.769
Mortimer Harren...

00:07:57.844 --> 00:08:01.803
William Telfer, Tal Celes...
none of them.

00:08:01.881 --> 00:08:04.645
They get off the ship
whenever we have general leave.

00:08:04.717 --> 00:08:06.651
I mean a working away mission.

00:08:06.719 --> 00:08:08.414
Harren never volunteers,

00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:11.514
Celes can't get past
the proficiency requirements,

00:08:11.591 --> 00:08:14.856
and Telfer always seems
to get a note from his doctor.

00:08:14.927 --> 00:08:16.622
Something's got to be done
about this.

00:08:16.696 --> 00:08:17.628
What can we do?

00:08:17.697 --> 00:08:18.891
There are always a few

00:08:18.965 --> 00:08:21.297
who don't make it past
their first year on a starship.

00:08:21.367 --> 00:08:22.891
Normally, they're reassigned.

00:08:23.002 --> 00:08:26.403
But in our case, maybe we
should relieve them of duty

00:08:26.472 --> 00:08:28.235
and let them pursue
their own interests.

00:08:28.307 --> 00:08:30.468
It certainly wouldn't hurt
general efficiency.

00:08:30.543 --> 00:08:33.671
They aren't drones, Chakotay.
We can't just deactivate them.

00:08:35.114 --> 00:08:37.275
Is the Delta Flyer ready?

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:40.683
Flight-checked with provisions
for a 72-hour away mission.

00:08:42.722 --> 00:08:44.519
What have you got in mind,
Captain?

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:52.863
Three people have slipped
through the cracks on my ship.

00:08:52.932 --> 00:08:55.867
That makes it my problem.

00:09:02.575 --> 00:09:03.769
The analytical aspects

00:09:03.843 --> 00:09:06.311
of the subspace infrared
algorithm are fourfold.

00:09:06.379 --> 00:09:08.506
Unfortunately, I have
a threefold brain.

00:09:08.581 --> 00:09:10.242
You just have
to break it down.

00:09:10.316 --> 00:09:12.876
Think of it
as four smaller algorithms.

00:09:12.952 --> 00:09:14.442
Okay. But what's the sequence?

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:15.452
It's...

00:09:15.521 --> 00:09:17.011
Zero-G Is Fun.

00:09:17.089 --> 00:09:18.647
As you were.

00:09:21.093 --> 00:09:24.722
Zeta particle derivation.
Gamma wave frequency.

00:09:24.797 --> 00:09:27.288
Ion distribution.
Flow rate of positrons.

00:09:27.366 --> 00:09:29.891
Z.G.I. F... Zero-G Is Fun.

00:09:30.036 --> 00:09:32.163
That's how you remember
the sequence.

00:09:32.238 --> 00:09:33.728
Thank you, Captain.

00:09:33.806 --> 00:09:35.330
- I'll try.
- Good...

00:09:35.408 --> 00:09:37.638
because where we're headed,
you're going to need it.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:39.200
I'll be briefing you
this afternoon

00:09:39.278 --> 00:09:40.870
in Astrometrics.

00:09:40.947 --> 00:09:44.542
We'll leave first thing
in the morning.

00:09:53.726 --> 00:09:55.523
Deck 15.

00:10:15.314 --> 00:10:17.475
Captain on the deck!

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:19.040
At ease.

00:10:21.921 --> 00:10:23.286
Junction Room 16?

00:10:23.356 --> 00:10:24.448
Over there, Captain.

00:10:24.523 --> 00:10:25.490
Of course.

00:10:27.526 --> 00:10:30.825
Crewman Mitchell,
how have you been?

00:10:31.897 --> 00:10:33.762
Uh, never better, ma'am.

00:10:33.833 --> 00:10:35.266
Yourself?

00:10:35.334 --> 00:10:39.293
Not bad. Not bad at all.

00:10:43.476 --> 00:10:44.966
Uh, to the left, ma'am.

00:10:45.077 --> 00:10:47.102
Thank you.

00:10:56.889 --> 00:10:58.322
Crewman Harren.

00:10:59.392 --> 00:11:02.293
Captain Janeway... are you lost?

00:11:02.361 --> 00:11:04.852
I was, for a minute.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:07.524
I'll be briefing you
this afternoon.

00:11:09.468 --> 00:11:11.459
Well, there's been a mistake.

00:11:11.537 --> 00:11:13.095
Excuse me?

00:11:13.172 --> 00:11:15.572
You have me assigned
to an away mission.

00:11:15.641 --> 00:11:18.701
I have my duties here.
I'd prefer not to leave my post.

00:11:18.778 --> 00:11:20.507
Ensign Culhane
will cover for you.

00:11:20.579 --> 00:11:22.513
The preflight schedule
is all there.

00:11:24.216 --> 00:11:28.277
If this is charity, Captain,
I don't want it.

00:11:28.354 --> 00:11:31.152
I didn't ask you what you want.

00:11:31.223 --> 00:11:32.884
I'm taking the Delta Flyer

00:11:32.958 --> 00:11:34.949
on an astronomical
survey mission,

00:11:35.094 --> 00:11:36.891
and your expertise is needed.

00:11:36.962 --> 00:11:39.192
What do you know
about my expertise?

00:11:39.265 --> 00:11:41.893
As much as I need to.

00:11:41.967 --> 00:11:44.458
Well, then you might be
interested to know

00:11:44.537 --> 00:11:45.868
that I'm about to disprove

00:11:45.938 --> 00:11:48.202
Schlezholt's theory
of multiple big bangs.

00:11:48.274 --> 00:11:49.764
Really?

00:11:49.842 --> 00:11:52.970
Wang's second postulate has more
lives than a cat, doesn't it?

00:11:53.045 --> 00:11:54.910
Once you think
you've eliminated it,

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:56.470
bam, it pops up again.

00:11:56.549 --> 00:11:58.540
I'll give you a hand,
if you'd like,

00:11:58.617 --> 00:12:01.711
when the away mission is over.

00:12:16.836 --> 00:12:18.303
Once we reach the cluster,

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:20.429
we'll drop out of warp
and maintain

00:12:20.506 --> 00:12:21.495
one-quarter impulse

00:12:21.574 --> 00:12:23.508
on the sweep through
the protostars.

00:12:23.576 --> 00:12:25.339
I'll be piloting
the Delta Flyer.

00:12:25.411 --> 00:12:26.708
Celes, you're going

00:12:26.779 --> 00:12:28.804
to run an ongoing
sensor analysis,

00:12:28.881 --> 00:12:31.179
providing data for
your colleagues.

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:32.547
Mr. Harren, you'll be looking

00:12:32.618 --> 00:12:34.085
at subspace particle decay

00:12:34.153 --> 00:12:38.112
for anything new we might learn
about star formation.

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:39.521
And, Mr. Telfer,

00:12:39.592 --> 00:12:42.152
your job will be to
look for signs of life,

00:12:42.228 --> 00:12:43.957
a long shot in this environment.

00:12:44.096 --> 00:12:47.964
But if it's out there,
I'm sure you'll find it.

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:49.625
You'll have the
rest of the evening

00:12:49.702 --> 00:12:51.693
to familiarize yourselves
with the mission.

00:12:51.771 --> 00:12:52.760
Excuse me, Captain.

00:12:52.838 --> 00:12:55.363
If we find a planet,
we're not planning

00:12:55.441 --> 00:12:57.432
on exploring the surface,
are we?

00:12:57.510 --> 00:12:58.977
That's a stellar nursery.

00:12:59.044 --> 00:13:00.944
Any planets will be gas giants.

00:13:01.013 --> 00:13:02.139
They may have moons.

00:13:02.214 --> 00:13:03.374
Don't worry.

00:13:03.449 --> 00:13:05.383
We'll run a complete scan
for pathogens

00:13:05.451 --> 00:13:06.850
before we set foot anywhere,

00:13:06.919 --> 00:13:08.784
and the Delta Flyer
is fully equipped

00:13:08.854 --> 00:13:10.719
to deal with
medical emergencies.

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:12.724
We'll be fine.

00:13:12.792 --> 00:13:16.489
Shuttle Bay 1, 0600 hours.

00:13:16.562 --> 00:13:18.029
Dismissed.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:26.936
Celes is unreliable.

00:13:27.006 --> 00:13:29.600
Her sensor analyses
will be full of errors.

00:13:29.675 --> 00:13:31.609
You could be putting
your lives at risk.

00:13:31.677 --> 00:13:33.611
Don't worry, Seven,
I'll check her work.

00:13:33.679 --> 00:13:35.613
This mission could be
better served

00:13:35.681 --> 00:13:37.342
with a more experienced crew.

00:13:37.416 --> 00:13:38.940
No...

00:13:39.084 --> 00:13:40.346
not this mission.

00:13:40.419 --> 00:13:43.479
Ever hear the tale
of the Good Shepherd?

00:13:43.556 --> 00:13:47.048
If even one sheep strayed
into the wilderness,

00:13:47.126 --> 00:13:50.289
the shepherd left the
safety of the flock

00:13:50.362 --> 00:13:51.761
and went after it.

00:13:51.831 --> 00:13:54.959
So, you're intending
to rescue them?

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.829
In a manner of speaking.

00:13:56.902 --> 00:13:58.631
Maybe all it will take will be

00:13:58.704 --> 00:14:01.434
some personal attention
from their Captain,

00:14:01.507 --> 00:14:03.737
maybe something more,

00:14:03.809 --> 00:14:07.575
but I won't abandon
a member of this crew,

00:14:07.646 --> 00:14:10.137
no matter what their problems
might be.

00:14:26.999 --> 00:14:29.661
Poor guy...

00:14:29.735 --> 00:14:31.396
rotting away down on Deck 15,

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:33.836
counting the years
till we get out

00:14:33.906 --> 00:14:35.533
of this godforsaken Quadrant.

00:14:35.608 --> 00:14:36.768
It's a shame he doesn't have

00:14:36.842 --> 00:14:38.469
a superior officer who cares.

00:14:38.544 --> 00:14:39.806
It's not my job

00:14:39.879 --> 00:14:42.848
to make everybody
who works for me happy.

00:14:42.915 --> 00:14:45.679
Some people just
don't want to fit in.

00:14:45.751 --> 00:14:48.242
I'll bet you haven't
said two words to him.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:50.618
Two words, exactly.

00:14:50.689 --> 00:14:53.123
We collided in the corridor
during a Borg attack.

00:14:53.192 --> 00:14:54.819
I said, "Excuse me."

00:14:54.894 --> 00:14:56.953
Since we were at Red Alert

00:14:57.096 --> 00:14:57.960
and about to be destroyed,

00:14:58.097 --> 00:14:59.359
I think it was
very considerate of me.

00:14:59.431 --> 00:15:00.523
Well, Mr. Considerate,

00:15:00.599 --> 00:15:01.691
why don't you go over there

00:15:01.767 --> 00:15:05.828
right now and offer
him some encouragement?

00:15:05.905 --> 00:15:07.805
His first away mission.

00:15:07.873 --> 00:15:09.670
I'm sure he could use it.

00:15:19.385 --> 00:15:21.615
Brushing up
on the Delta Flyer specs?

00:15:24.223 --> 00:15:25.884
I'm not a mechanic.

00:15:25.958 --> 00:15:28.017
Oh.

00:15:28.093 --> 00:15:30.960
Then, what are you doing?

00:15:40.005 --> 00:15:42.599
Very interesting.

00:15:42.675 --> 00:15:45.872
What do you find
most interesting about it?

00:15:48.247 --> 00:15:51.045
Your creative use
of the minus sign.

00:15:53.252 --> 00:15:55.618
I see you have
a, uh, appreciation

00:15:55.688 --> 00:15:57.588
for multivariate analysis.

00:15:57.656 --> 00:15:59.817
Maybe you missed
your calling.

00:15:59.892 --> 00:16:01.291
It's a shame.

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:03.885
I imagine it gets tedious
up at the helm.

00:16:04.029 --> 00:16:07.430
I enjoy the view.

00:16:12.638 --> 00:16:13.900
Well?

00:16:14.039 --> 00:16:18.237
I invited him over to watch
our television set tonight.

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:20.437
You don't mind, do you?

00:16:26.585 --> 00:16:28.075
Celes, Celes...

00:16:29.989 --> 00:16:32.685
Respond. Celes, respond.

00:16:36.061 --> 00:16:37.494
You're not sick.

00:16:37.563 --> 00:16:39.155
Yes, I am.

00:16:39.231 --> 00:16:40.357
No, you're not.

00:16:40.432 --> 00:16:41.364
Really...

00:16:41.433 --> 00:16:42.365
I am.

00:16:42.434 --> 00:16:43.366
We have to sleep.

00:16:43.435 --> 00:16:45.733
I can't go on this mission.

00:16:45.804 --> 00:16:46.736
Yes, you can.

00:16:46.805 --> 00:16:47.737
No, I can't.

00:16:47.806 --> 00:16:48.864
- Yes.
- No.

00:16:48.941 --> 00:16:50.033
Bye.

00:16:50.109 --> 00:16:50.700
Wait.

00:16:54.446 --> 00:16:56.209
See?

00:16:56.281 --> 00:16:57.213
It's nothing.

00:16:57.282 --> 00:16:58.214
It's a fever.

00:16:58.283 --> 00:17:00.444
Your temperature is
.2 degrees above normal.

00:17:00.519 --> 00:17:01.884
That's right.

00:17:02.021 --> 00:17:03.079
A typical deviation

00:17:03.155 --> 00:17:05.214
easily prompted by
emotional stress.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:07.281
Or a multiphasic prion.

00:17:07.359 --> 00:17:09.554
You have not been infected
by a prion.

00:17:09.628 --> 00:17:10.560
They attach themselves

00:17:10.629 --> 00:17:12.324
to the mitochondrial walls,
and they just...

00:17:12.398 --> 00:17:13.365
I've already scanned you.

00:17:13.432 --> 00:17:15.332
You can barely see them.

00:17:15.401 --> 00:17:16.732
They aren't there.

00:17:16.802 --> 00:17:18.360
If they migrate
to my cell membranes

00:17:18.437 --> 00:17:21.031
while I'm on the away mission,
they could rupture and I...

00:17:21.106 --> 00:17:24.303
Crewman, I am not giving
you a medical excuse...

00:17:24.376 --> 00:17:25.809
not this time.

00:17:25.878 --> 00:17:28.312
Try to get some sleep.

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:31.008
You shouldn't even have
a medical tricorder.

00:17:32.051 --> 00:17:33.313
Believe me...

00:17:33.385 --> 00:17:36.081
you'll be so caught up in
the excitement of exploration,

00:17:36.155 --> 00:17:39.591
there won't be any time
for worrying about infections,

00:17:39.658 --> 00:17:41.626
mitochondrial
or otherwise.

00:17:41.693 --> 00:17:43.593
There's nothing like
an away mission

00:17:43.662 --> 00:17:46.790
to remind a person
of why we're out here.

00:17:57.009 --> 00:17:58.943
I'm going
to one-quarter impulse.

00:17:59.011 --> 00:18:01.104
Should I start
the sensor sweeps?

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:03.614
We don't want to miss anything.

00:18:03.682 --> 00:18:05.115
Engine status?

00:18:05.184 --> 00:18:06.446
Within parameters.

00:18:06.518 --> 00:18:07.780
That wasn't us.

00:18:07.853 --> 00:18:09.286
Anything on sensors?

00:18:09.354 --> 00:18:12.846
.005 fluctuation in
the spatial continuum.

00:18:12.925 --> 00:18:15.393
It looks like simple
background noise.

00:18:17.863 --> 00:18:18.795
I agree.

00:18:18.864 --> 00:18:20.331
Anybody for lunch?

00:18:20.399 --> 00:18:22.128
Are you volunteering, William?

00:18:22.201 --> 00:18:23.133
Yes, ma'am.

00:18:23.202 --> 00:18:24.134
I'll help.

00:18:24.203 --> 00:18:25.465
What would you like, Captain?

00:18:25.537 --> 00:18:26.469
Mortimer?

00:18:26.538 --> 00:18:29.701
Even my mother
didn't call me that.

00:18:29.775 --> 00:18:32.266
Well, then, Mr. Harren,
are you hungry?

00:18:32.344 --> 00:18:33.606
No.

00:18:33.679 --> 00:18:35.476
Thank you.

00:18:35.547 --> 00:18:37.412
I'll have the pasta soup.

00:18:37.483 --> 00:18:40.475
It should be listed
under Neelix 651.

00:18:40.552 --> 00:18:42.144
Maybe I'll try that, too.

00:18:42.221 --> 00:18:43.916
I'm sure you'll like it.

00:18:44.056 --> 00:18:44.920
I'm sure I will.

00:18:45.057 --> 00:18:46.718
Thanks for the suggestion.

00:18:50.395 --> 00:18:51.885
I'd better get back there.

00:18:57.336 --> 00:19:00.203
Neelix 651, two servings.

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:05.276
Neelix 651, two servings.

00:19:05.344 --> 00:19:07.938
What's wrong?

00:19:09.348 --> 00:19:12.249
The Captain checks
every single thing I do.

00:19:12.317 --> 00:19:15.286
Oh... that's
just standard procedure.

00:19:15.354 --> 00:19:16.719
Then, why isn't it
standard procedure

00:19:16.788 --> 00:19:18.221
for you or Harren?

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:20.622
Maybe she's giving you
special attention.

00:19:20.692 --> 00:19:22.922
Yeah, because she
knows I need it.

00:19:24.229 --> 00:19:27.062
I wish I could go
back to Voyager.

00:19:27.132 --> 00:19:29.896
Me, too.

00:19:29.968 --> 00:19:32.300
There's always the escape pods.

00:19:32.371 --> 00:19:34.805
Can you imagine?

00:19:36.175 --> 00:19:38.803
I understand you grew up
on Vico V.

00:19:38.877 --> 00:19:41.311
No wonder you became
a cosmologist.

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:44.406
Wildest sky in
the Alpha Quadrant.

00:19:44.483 --> 00:19:46.007
So they say.
I've never been there.

00:19:46.084 --> 00:19:47.346
Do you really believe

00:19:47.419 --> 00:19:49.216
that childhood environment
is more important

00:19:49.288 --> 00:19:51.051
than genetically driven
behavior patterns?

00:19:51.123 --> 00:19:54.183
Just making conversation.

00:19:54.259 --> 00:19:56.750
Conversation filled
with unspoken assumptions,

00:19:56.828 --> 00:19:58.227
which I don't agree with.

00:19:58.297 --> 00:19:59.924
I'm a product of
my nucleic acids.

00:20:00.065 --> 00:20:01.362
Where and how I was raised

00:20:01.433 --> 00:20:02.695
are beside the point,

00:20:02.768 --> 00:20:05.066
so if you're trying
to understand me better,

00:20:05.137 --> 00:20:07.571
questions about my home planet
are irrelevant.

00:20:07.639 --> 00:20:10.403
All right, then.

00:20:10.475 --> 00:20:12.443
How's your 13th chromosome?

00:20:12.511 --> 00:20:16.413
Missing a couple of base pairs
in gene 178?

00:20:19.251 --> 00:20:21.310
I signed onto Voyager
because I needed a year

00:20:21.386 --> 00:20:22.944
of hands-on experience.

00:20:23.055 --> 00:20:24.283
It was a requirement for getting

00:20:24.356 --> 00:20:27.257
into the Institute of Cosmology
on Orion I.

00:20:27.326 --> 00:20:30.489
If we hadn't gotten lost
in the Delta Quadrant,

00:20:30.562 --> 00:20:32.496
I'd be there right now.

00:20:32.564 --> 00:20:34.794
Sorry to have delayed
your career plans,

00:20:34.866 --> 00:20:37.494
but all of us have had
our lives interrupted.

00:20:37.569 --> 00:20:39.833
That's the nature
of space exploration.

00:20:39.905 --> 00:20:40.963
It's unpredictable.

00:20:41.073 --> 00:20:44.133
Which is why I don't
like space exploration.

00:20:44.209 --> 00:20:47.667
Stumbling from star to star
like a-a drunken insect

00:20:47.746 --> 00:20:49.873
careening toward a light source

00:20:49.948 --> 00:20:52.746
is not my idea
of a dignified existence.

00:20:52.818 --> 00:20:55.309
Pure theory is all
that concerns me.

00:20:55.387 --> 00:20:58.151
Well, I'm not trying
to change that.

00:20:58.223 --> 00:21:01.021
I'm simply trying to get
every member of my crew working

00:21:01.093 --> 00:21:02.355
to their full capacity.

00:21:02.427 --> 00:21:04.088
That includes you, Mr. Harren.

00:21:04.162 --> 00:21:06.926
You don't feel responsible,
Captain...

00:21:07.032 --> 00:21:08.863
for having three misfits

00:21:08.934 --> 00:21:09.866
aboard your ship?

00:21:09.935 --> 00:21:11.527
Well, if there's
anything I can do

00:21:11.603 --> 00:21:14.094
to help relieve your guilt...

00:21:14.172 --> 00:21:15.867
please let me know.

00:21:15.941 --> 00:21:19.138
I'll keep that in mind.

00:21:22.347 --> 00:21:25.441
Maybe I will join my
colleagues for lunch.

00:21:25.517 --> 00:21:28.975
All this exploration
has given me an appetite.

00:21:39.264 --> 00:21:42.961
Computer, identify the source
of that spatial fluctuation.

00:21:43.101 --> 00:21:44.398
Source unknown.

00:21:49.041 --> 00:21:50.975
Red Alert!

00:21:51.043 --> 00:21:52.510
Aft section, report!

00:21:53.545 --> 00:21:54.910
Report!

00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:03.117
Captain, are you all right?

00:22:03.188 --> 00:22:04.587
We need to get
propulsion back on line

00:22:04.656 --> 00:22:07.056
and figure out what hit us.

00:22:07.125 --> 00:22:08.319
What's out there?

00:22:08.393 --> 00:22:09.758
I don't know,

00:22:09.828 --> 00:22:11.318
but whatever it was,
it tore a plating section

00:22:11.396 --> 00:22:12.454
off the outer hull.

00:22:12.531 --> 00:22:15.056
90 percent of our antimatter's
been neutralized.

00:22:15.133 --> 00:22:16.361
The reaction's cold.

00:22:16.435 --> 00:22:18.027
So much for warp drive.

00:22:18.103 --> 00:22:19.798
I'm bringing
the impulse engines on line,

00:22:19.871 --> 00:22:21.930
but they've been damaged.

00:22:22.007 --> 00:22:24.840
We'll be able to do
one-eighth impulse, no more.

00:22:24.910 --> 00:22:26.707
That should get us
to the rendezvous point

00:22:26.778 --> 00:22:28.609
with Voyager in about ten years.

00:22:28.680 --> 00:22:30.272
Think they'll wait for us?

00:22:30.349 --> 00:22:31.714
Is the subspace

00:22:31.783 --> 00:22:33.944
transmitter on line?

00:22:34.086 --> 00:22:35.747
Voyager, this is
the Delta Flyer.

00:22:35.821 --> 00:22:37.618
We've been hit
by an unknown phenomenon

00:22:37.689 --> 00:22:38.621
and taken heavy damage.

00:22:38.690 --> 00:22:40.453
We require
immediate assistance.

00:22:40.525 --> 00:22:42.959
Repeat: We require
immediate assistance.

00:22:43.028 --> 00:22:46.122
Transmit that continuously
on all subspace frequencies.

00:22:46.198 --> 00:22:47.563
Anything on active scans?

00:22:47.632 --> 00:22:48.894
Not yet.

00:22:48.967 --> 00:22:50.400
It was a dark-matter
protocomet.

00:22:50.469 --> 00:22:52.300
I read a paper
on that phenomenon once.

00:22:52.371 --> 00:22:53.395
Written by me.

00:22:53.472 --> 00:22:55.963
Well, enlighten us,
Mr. Harren.

00:22:56.041 --> 00:22:58.976
I hypothesized
that a tertiary product

00:22:59.044 --> 00:23:00.636
of stellar consolidation
would be

00:23:00.712 --> 00:23:03.078
a comet-like assemblage
of dark matter.

00:23:03.148 --> 00:23:05.082
It would be attracted
to any source of antimatter

00:23:05.150 --> 00:23:07.015
and neutralize it
upon contact.

00:23:07.085 --> 00:23:09.918
So, one of these things detected
the antimatter in our warp core?

00:23:09.988 --> 00:23:12.149
The term "detected" suggests
a consciousness.

00:23:12.224 --> 00:23:14.317
This is a mindless
astrophysical phenomenon,

00:23:14.393 --> 00:23:15.485
nothing more.

00:23:15.560 --> 00:23:17.528
We should eject
our remaining antimatter

00:23:17.596 --> 00:23:19.257
or we could suffer
another impact.

00:23:19.331 --> 00:23:20.263
I can't do that,

00:23:20.332 --> 00:23:22.857
not on the basis
of an unproven hypothesis.

00:23:22.934 --> 00:23:24.060
The forces involved

00:23:24.136 --> 00:23:25.763
are nontrivial...
if we're hit again,

00:23:25.837 --> 00:23:27.702
we could lose
our entire outer hull.

00:23:27.773 --> 00:23:29.172
Eject the warp core,

00:23:29.241 --> 00:23:31.232
and we lose any hope
of getting warp drive back.

00:23:31.309 --> 00:23:32.241
I need more evidence,

00:23:32.310 --> 00:23:34.175
and right now,
sensors aren't talking.

00:23:34.246 --> 00:23:35.611
Maybe they are talking,

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:38.706
but somebody doesn't know
how to listen to them.

00:23:38.784 --> 00:23:39.614
You're out of line, crewman.

00:23:39.684 --> 00:23:40.946
This isn't the time
to be worried

00:23:41.086 --> 00:23:42.280
about her feelings, Captain.

00:23:42.354 --> 00:23:43.286
We're in trouble.

00:23:43.355 --> 00:23:44.287
Captain, that hull plate...

00:23:44.356 --> 00:23:46.620
it's less
than ten kilometers away.

00:23:46.691 --> 00:23:47.851
Impact from a dark-matter body

00:23:47.926 --> 00:23:50.121
might've left a quantum
signature in the alloys.

00:23:50.195 --> 00:23:52.220
That's the evidence
we're looking for.

00:23:52.297 --> 00:23:53.525
Do we have transporters?

00:23:53.598 --> 00:23:54.963
Yes, I've locked on
to the plate.

00:23:55.033 --> 00:23:56.898
Beam it directly
to the aft section.

00:23:56.968 --> 00:23:58.333
Celes, you're with me.

00:23:58.403 --> 00:23:59.836
Continue the repairs.

00:24:08.046 --> 00:24:11.641
No sign of burns...

00:24:11.716 --> 00:24:13.775
or plasma residue.

00:24:16.388 --> 00:24:18.913
It seems to have been
sheared off.

00:24:18.990 --> 00:24:21.618
Download this
into the main computer.

00:24:31.169 --> 00:24:32.568
Captain, I'm sorry.

00:24:32.637 --> 00:24:33.797
For what?

00:24:33.872 --> 00:24:36.102
I thought
that spatial fluctuation

00:24:36.174 --> 00:24:38.108
we ran into was
background noise.

00:24:38.176 --> 00:24:39.643
Some noise.

00:24:39.711 --> 00:24:41.770
I saw the same
sensor readings you did

00:24:41.847 --> 00:24:43.610
and came
to the same conclusion.

00:24:43.682 --> 00:24:46.242
You don't have to doubt
yourself all the time.

00:24:46.318 --> 00:24:48.081
Yes, I do, and you should, too.

00:24:48.153 --> 00:24:51.122
You're right to always be
looking over my shoulder.

00:24:51.189 --> 00:24:54.056
We all make mistakes, even me.

00:24:54.125 --> 00:24:55.149
Every day?

00:24:55.227 --> 00:24:58.628
Every time you report for duty?

00:24:58.697 --> 00:25:00.289
On Voyager, it doesn't matter,

00:25:00.365 --> 00:25:02.230
because nothing I
do is that critical.

00:25:02.300 --> 00:25:04.894
Seven doesn't trust me
with anything important.

00:25:04.970 --> 00:25:07.234
The crew is protected
from my mistakes

00:25:07.305 --> 00:25:09.273
by the people around me, but...

00:25:09.341 --> 00:25:11.332
out here I could get us killed.

00:25:11.409 --> 00:25:14.537
You went through
Starfleet training courses.

00:25:14.613 --> 00:25:17.104
I had to cram for every exam.

00:25:17.182 --> 00:25:20.515
At the Academy, I was infamous
for my all-nighters.

00:25:20.585 --> 00:25:23.918
Every night?
Because that's what it took.

00:25:23.989 --> 00:25:26.082
That's the only way
I made it through.

00:25:26.157 --> 00:25:28.853
Not to mention
the sympathy votes.

00:25:28.927 --> 00:25:31.293
The conflict on Bajor
worked in my favor.

00:25:31.363 --> 00:25:32.887
The Federation was so eager

00:25:32.964 --> 00:25:34.158
to have Bajorans in Starfleet

00:25:34.232 --> 00:25:37.292
that my instructors gave me
the benefit of the doubt.

00:25:37.369 --> 00:25:39.735
So did you, when you accepted

00:25:39.804 --> 00:25:40.930
my application.

00:25:41.006 --> 00:25:43.099
You showed evidence
of unconventional thinking.

00:25:43.174 --> 00:25:44.607
I liked that.

00:25:44.676 --> 00:25:48.203
Not everybody would've thought
to retrieve that hull plating.

00:25:48.280 --> 00:25:50.248
Well, just don't trust me
with the analysis.

00:25:50.315 --> 00:25:51.714
I guarantee I'll get it wrong.

00:25:51.783 --> 00:25:53.842
Well, with that attitude,
I'm sure you will.

00:25:53.919 --> 00:25:56.911
This has nothing to do
with attitude, Captain.

00:25:56.988 --> 00:25:59.115
You and I are wired differently.

00:25:59.190 --> 00:26:01.317
To you,
this is nothing but data.

00:26:01.393 --> 00:26:06.023
To me, it... it's a monster
with-with fangs and claws.

00:26:07.632 --> 00:26:11.068
In my nightmares,
I am chased by algorithms.

00:26:11.136 --> 00:26:13.900
My brain just wasn't built
to understand this.

00:26:14.039 --> 00:26:18.533
We can find you
another post on Voyager.

00:26:18.610 --> 00:26:22.273
There isn't another post
on Voyager, not for me...

00:26:22.347 --> 00:26:25.748
unless you need a waitress
in the Mess Hall.

00:26:25.817 --> 00:26:28.911
You know...

00:26:28.987 --> 00:26:30.750
there's more to duty
than the ability

00:26:30.822 --> 00:26:33.256
to manipulate algorithms.

00:26:33.325 --> 00:26:35.589
Everybody on Voyager has showed

00:26:35.660 --> 00:26:38.595
a courage far beyond
what I could've expected.

00:26:38.663 --> 00:26:40.563
So have you.

00:26:40.632 --> 00:26:42.429
If we were still
in the Alpha Quadrant,

00:26:42.500 --> 00:26:45.401
would that be enough
to keep me on board?

00:26:47.005 --> 00:26:48.905
I can't answer that.

00:26:48.974 --> 00:26:52.239
I don't deserve to be
on your ship, Captain.

00:26:52.310 --> 00:26:55.074
And I'm not really a part
of Voyager.

00:26:55.146 --> 00:26:57.307
I just live there.

00:27:03.955 --> 00:27:06.219
Pressure's increasing.
The EPS relays are fused.

00:27:06.291 --> 00:27:08.782
Cut the plasma flow.

00:27:08.860 --> 00:27:10.623
Cut the plasma!

00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:17.594
I could've been killed.
What's wrong with you?

00:27:17.669 --> 00:27:19.432
Everything.

00:27:19.504 --> 00:27:22.735
If you want something
to fantasize about,

00:27:22.807 --> 00:27:24.741
try imagining how it'll feel
if our hull is breached

00:27:24.809 --> 00:27:26.470
and we die of vacuum exposure.

00:27:26.544 --> 00:27:27.909
Our blood will vaporize,

00:27:28.013 --> 00:27:30.311
and our cell membranes
will rupture.

00:27:30.382 --> 00:27:32.441
Surely you know the symptoms
better than I do.

00:27:32.517 --> 00:27:34.644
Let's not talk about
it, all right?

00:27:34.719 --> 00:27:36.277
Nothing disagrees with me

00:27:36.354 --> 00:27:38.914
more than having to put theories
into practical use,

00:27:39.057 --> 00:27:40.354
but there's no choice,

00:27:40.425 --> 00:27:42.484
so pay attention
to what we're doing here.

00:27:42.560 --> 00:27:44.926
You can check yourself
into Sick Bay when we get back.

00:27:45.030 --> 00:27:46.827
And you can go back to Deck 15.

00:27:47.899 --> 00:27:49.423
That's right...

00:27:49.501 --> 00:27:50.934
where I don't have
to rely on you

00:27:51.002 --> 00:27:53.402
or your intellectually
deficient friend.

00:27:53.471 --> 00:27:56.702
At least I have a friend.

00:27:59.744 --> 00:28:02.679
Don't you ever get
lonely down there?

00:28:02.747 --> 00:28:05.443
In the company
of my own thoughts?

00:28:05.517 --> 00:28:07.883
Never.

00:28:07.952 --> 00:28:10.250
I don't believe that.

00:28:10.321 --> 00:28:13.290
Spend some time with us
when we get back.

00:28:13.358 --> 00:28:15.417
You might enjoy yourself.

00:28:15.493 --> 00:28:18.758
A hypothesis
that would require testing.

00:28:18.830 --> 00:28:21.458
I'm a theoretician, remember?

00:28:21.533 --> 00:28:26.232
Captain's Log, Delta Flyer,
Stardate 53764.3.

00:28:26.304 --> 00:28:28.738
We've been running
on minimal power for six hours.

00:28:28.807 --> 00:28:30.399
Still no response
to our distress call,

00:28:30.475 --> 00:28:33.410
and no answers from
the computer on what hit us.

00:28:33.478 --> 00:28:35.503
For now, it looks like
we're on our own.

00:28:35.580 --> 00:28:38.276
Our scans of the hull fragment
were inconclusive.

00:28:38.349 --> 00:28:40.112
We found
some displaced positrons

00:28:40.185 --> 00:28:42.449
that could indicate
a dark-matter impact.

00:28:42.520 --> 00:28:44.715
But could've been caused
by something else?

00:28:44.789 --> 00:28:45.756
Proof enough.

00:28:45.824 --> 00:28:47.257
Not enough for me.

00:28:47.325 --> 00:28:50.590
Not enough to jettison
the remaining antimatter.

00:28:50.662 --> 00:28:51.924
There's a gas giant

00:28:51.996 --> 00:28:54.464
only a few hours
from our current position.

00:28:54.532 --> 00:28:57.057
T-class, surrounded
by orbital rings,

00:28:57.135 --> 00:28:59.262
including one that's radiogenic.

00:28:59.337 --> 00:29:01.271
We could use those particles

00:29:01.339 --> 00:29:03.637
to reinitialize
our warp reaction.

00:29:03.708 --> 00:29:05.539
With ten percent of
our antimatter left,

00:29:05.610 --> 00:29:07.237
we'd only be able
to make warp 2,

00:29:07.312 --> 00:29:09.746
but it would be enough to
get us back on the road.

00:29:09.848 --> 00:29:11.145
Set a course.

00:29:16.454 --> 00:29:18.149
Another spatial fluctuation.

00:29:18.223 --> 00:29:19.520
Can you localize it?

00:29:19.591 --> 00:29:22.685
It's somewhere within
the distance

00:29:22.761 --> 00:29:24.729
of 10,000 kilometers.

00:29:24.796 --> 00:29:27.890
Another one, closer,
about 7,000 kilometers.

00:29:27.966 --> 00:29:29.558
It's being drawn
toward our antimatter.

00:29:29.634 --> 00:29:30.726
Eject the core.

00:29:30.802 --> 00:29:33.327
Open a channel.
All hailing frequencies.

00:29:35.039 --> 00:29:38.008
This is Captain Janeway of the
Federation Vessel Delta Flyer.

00:29:38.076 --> 00:29:40.909
We are on a mission
of peaceful exploration.

00:29:41.012 --> 00:29:43.776
Please identify yourself.

00:29:45.717 --> 00:29:48.117
No response.

00:29:48.186 --> 00:29:49.915
Of course not.
It's a natural phenomenon.

00:29:49.988 --> 00:29:51.216
Captain, we only have
a few seconds.

00:29:51.289 --> 00:29:54.087
I'm firing a photon torpedo.

00:29:54.159 --> 00:29:55.922
There's enough antimatter
in the detonation chamber

00:29:56.027 --> 00:29:58.928
to draw that protocomet,
if that's what it is.

00:30:01.499 --> 00:30:03.023
The torpedo's away.

00:30:03.101 --> 00:30:05.934
Distance: 1,000 kilometers.

00:30:06.037 --> 00:30:08.301
1,500.

00:30:08.373 --> 00:30:10.170
No spatial disruptions.

00:30:11.242 --> 00:30:14.370
Find the source of that sound.

00:30:26.157 --> 00:30:27.488
Oh, no.

00:30:30.428 --> 00:30:31.861
That's not possible.

00:30:31.930 --> 00:30:34.057
Where is he?

00:30:34.132 --> 00:30:36.430
I can't locate
his bio-signature.

00:30:36.501 --> 00:30:37.832
He's not out there.

00:30:37.902 --> 00:30:40.268
He's not in space,
not in subspace.

00:30:40.338 --> 00:30:41.669
It doesn't make sense.

00:30:49.848 --> 00:30:53.375
Inside... me...

00:31:01.993 --> 00:31:03.085
Activate the transporter.

00:31:03.161 --> 00:31:06.324
Try to get a lock
on whatever's inside him.

00:31:16.341 --> 00:31:18.468
Tricorder isn't
picking up anything.

00:31:18.543 --> 00:31:19.840
But I can feel it.

00:31:19.911 --> 00:31:21.276
I-I can't get a lock.

00:31:21.346 --> 00:31:23.507
It's like something's there,
but it's not there.

00:31:23.581 --> 00:31:24.980
Oh, it's there.

00:31:26.818 --> 00:31:29.184
Unfortunately, I have to agree.

00:31:29.254 --> 00:31:32.189
Obviously, whatever hit us
was no protocomet. I was wrong.

00:31:32.257 --> 00:31:33.849
Maybe you weren't, not entirely.

00:31:33.925 --> 00:31:35.085
Sensors can't scan it;

00:31:35.159 --> 00:31:37.423
transporters
can't lock on to it.

00:31:37.495 --> 00:31:40.259
Maybe this is some kind
of dark-matter life-form.

00:31:40.331 --> 00:31:41.263
That's impossible.

00:31:41.332 --> 00:31:42.458
Molecules that complex

00:31:42.533 --> 00:31:44.091
would collapse
under their own weight.

00:31:44.168 --> 00:31:45.430
They could never support life.

00:31:45.503 --> 00:31:47.403
Might be time
to revise your theory.

00:31:47.472 --> 00:31:48.530
Where did they take you?

00:31:48.606 --> 00:31:50.972
I don't know.

00:31:51.042 --> 00:31:52.634
It was dark.

00:31:52.710 --> 00:31:54.769
God, I could feel breathing
all around me.

00:31:54.846 --> 00:31:56.973
Did anyone try to communicate
with you?

00:31:57.048 --> 00:31:58.208
I couldn't see.

00:31:58.283 --> 00:32:01.684
I tried to say something,
but there wasn't enough air.

00:32:01.753 --> 00:32:03.345
I tried to move,

00:32:03.421 --> 00:32:06.288
but something was pressing
down on me.

00:32:08.026 --> 00:32:10.017
The hypospray... tetrovaline.
It'll put me out.

00:32:10.094 --> 00:32:13.621
If I sedate you, it could
lower your immune response,

00:32:13.698 --> 00:32:15.563
and you need to stay conscious.

00:32:15.633 --> 00:32:16.759
Do you understand?

00:32:18.303 --> 00:32:20.396
Billy...

00:32:20.471 --> 00:32:22.871
if it wanted to kill you,
it would've done it by now.

00:32:22.941 --> 00:32:24.909
It never would've
sent you back here.

00:32:24.976 --> 00:32:27.308
Maybe it was trying
to scan you or something.

00:32:27.378 --> 00:32:31.439
If it wanted
to get to know me better...

00:32:31.516 --> 00:32:34.212
it should've just asked me out
for a drink.

00:32:39.123 --> 00:32:40.590
Celes.

00:32:49.067 --> 00:32:50.830
Keep an eye on him.

00:32:50.902 --> 00:32:52.199
Harren.

00:32:58.710 --> 00:33:00.234
I'm setting a course
for those rings.

00:33:00.311 --> 00:33:02.643
Shunt as much power as you can
to the impulse engines.

00:33:02.714 --> 00:33:04.238
We never should've
left Voyager.

00:33:04.315 --> 00:33:05.407
I've got news for you, crewman.

00:33:05.483 --> 00:33:07.417
Voyager isn't exactly
a safe haven.

00:33:07.485 --> 00:33:09.077
We've been chased
across the Quadrant

00:33:09.153 --> 00:33:11.246
by far worse
than whatever's out there...

00:33:11.322 --> 00:33:15.258
the Vidiians,
Species 8472, the Borg...

00:33:15.326 --> 00:33:18.523
but I guess if somebody's
hiding down on Deck 15,

00:33:18.596 --> 00:33:20.461
they may not be aware of it.

00:33:20.531 --> 00:33:22.624
I wasn't meant
to be an explorer.

00:33:22.700 --> 00:33:24.167
And I wasn't meant
to guide a ship

00:33:24.235 --> 00:33:25.429
across an unknown Quadrant.

00:33:25.503 --> 00:33:27.937
Then we're both victims
of circumstance.

00:33:28.072 --> 00:33:30.063
Oh, I've seen things
I've never imagined,

00:33:30.141 --> 00:33:32.769
grown closer to people
than I ever thought possible.

00:33:32.844 --> 00:33:34.402
I wouldn't call myself a victim,

00:33:34.479 --> 00:33:37.175
and I wouldn't trade
the last six years for anything.

00:33:37.248 --> 00:33:38.374
Then you've been deluded

00:33:38.449 --> 00:33:40.212
by the inexhaustible
human capacity

00:33:40.284 --> 00:33:42.184
to avoid the truth.

00:33:42.253 --> 00:33:44.483
You're the one hiding, not me.

00:33:44.555 --> 00:33:48.218
I've got you three more
percentage points of impulse.

00:33:48.292 --> 00:33:49.281
I'll take it.

00:33:49.360 --> 00:33:50.987
Setting a course.

00:33:56.567 --> 00:33:59.195
Isn't there any part of you
that feels a bond

00:33:59.270 --> 00:34:00.737
with the rest of us?

00:34:00.805 --> 00:34:02.830
When we escape
from the Borg or discover

00:34:02.907 --> 00:34:03.896
a new type of star,

00:34:03.975 --> 00:34:06.341
don't you feel
some pride of accomplishment?

00:34:06.411 --> 00:34:08.470
When you're in the Mess Hall,

00:34:08.546 --> 00:34:11.014
alone at your table
in the corner,

00:34:11.082 --> 00:34:14.813
don't you see
the friendships around you

00:34:14.886 --> 00:34:18.253
and wish even for a microsecond
you were part of them?

00:34:22.326 --> 00:34:25.056
You don't know me at all.

00:34:25.129 --> 00:34:26.721
No, but I'd like to.

00:34:26.798 --> 00:34:30.097
That was the whole point
of this mission.

00:34:31.936 --> 00:34:37.067
But I guess it hasn't
worked out like I planned.

00:34:37.141 --> 00:34:39.268
Incoming transmission.

00:34:39.343 --> 00:34:40.332
Source?

00:34:40.411 --> 00:34:41.935
It's a Starfleet frequency.

00:34:42.013 --> 00:34:43.640
Must be Voyager.

00:34:44.715 --> 00:34:46.910
...the Delta Flyer.
...phenomenon...

00:34:46.984 --> 00:34:49.179
...hit by an...
...heavy damage.

00:34:49.253 --> 00:34:51.915
Repeat: Require,
require immediate...

00:34:51.989 --> 00:34:54.787
immediate, immediate...
Flyer, Flyer, Flyer, Flyer...

00:34:54.859 --> 00:34:56.724
Subspace echo.

00:34:56.794 --> 00:35:00.753
Maybe not. There's a.005
deviation in the carrier wave.

00:35:00.832 --> 00:35:02.390
That's the same degree
of spatial fluctuation

00:35:02.467 --> 00:35:04.628
left by our pursuers.

00:35:04.702 --> 00:35:08.138
They're sending
our distress signal back to us.

00:35:08.206 --> 00:35:11.073
Modified. They might
be trying to communicate.

00:35:11.142 --> 00:35:12.507
... Delta Flyer, Flyer, Flyer.

00:35:12.577 --> 00:35:14.636
...hit by an unknown
phenomenon, unknown.

00:35:14.712 --> 00:35:15.906
They're taunting us.

00:35:16.047 --> 00:35:17.810
Not necessarily.

00:35:17.882 --> 00:35:19.543
Try to adjust the universal
translator for...

00:35:19.617 --> 00:35:20.584
Captain!

00:35:22.553 --> 00:35:24.919
He went right through
the force field.

00:35:24.989 --> 00:35:26.923
Billy, what are you doing?

00:35:27.024 --> 00:35:29.549
It's activating
my motor neurons.

00:35:29.627 --> 00:35:31.185
I can't make it stop.

00:35:31.262 --> 00:35:32.752
I'm sorry, Captain.

00:35:32.830 --> 00:35:36.288
You've got to stop it.

00:35:38.202 --> 00:35:39.260
No.

00:35:39.337 --> 00:35:41.771
It's okay, Billy, it's okay.

00:35:41.839 --> 00:35:43.568
It's okay.

00:35:45.376 --> 00:35:47.936
It's in here.

00:35:53.584 --> 00:35:55.074
It's tapping into our systems.

00:35:55.153 --> 00:35:58.145
Wait. It may be
trying to communicate.

00:36:05.997 --> 00:36:07.328
It's into our
environmental controls.

00:36:07.398 --> 00:36:08.365
We've got to stop it.

00:36:09.267 --> 00:36:09.961
Hold your fire!

00:36:12.904 --> 00:36:14.030
What the hell is wrong with you?

00:36:14.105 --> 00:36:15.834
It was trying to kill us.

00:36:15.907 --> 00:36:17.169
- You don't know that.
- We were at risk.

00:36:17.241 --> 00:36:18.367
I gave you a direct order.

00:36:18.442 --> 00:36:19.739
What if you were wrong?

00:36:19.810 --> 00:36:23.007
I could hear
its thoughts.

00:36:23.080 --> 00:36:25.071
Explain.

00:36:25.149 --> 00:36:26.707
When it left me...

00:36:26.784 --> 00:36:29.617
I could hear
what it was thinking.

00:36:29.687 --> 00:36:32.349
"Do not belong."

00:36:32.423 --> 00:36:34.914
That's what it said:
"Do not belong."

00:36:35.059 --> 00:36:36.890
We don't belong here.

00:36:36.961 --> 00:36:39.327
Or it didn't belong
in the Delta Flyer.

00:36:39.397 --> 00:36:42.764
Maybe that's why it was tapping
into the environmental controls.

00:36:42.833 --> 00:36:44.630
It was trying to survive
in a place

00:36:44.702 --> 00:36:46.135
it didn't belong.

00:36:46.204 --> 00:36:47.034
That's speculation.

00:36:47.104 --> 00:36:49.436
Based on direct observation.

00:36:49.507 --> 00:36:51.270
You murdered an alien being
and destroyed

00:36:51.342 --> 00:36:54.834
any chance we had
to make first contact.

00:36:58.015 --> 00:37:00.142
We just lost
another section of hull.

00:37:00.218 --> 00:37:02.015
How far are we
from the gas giant?

00:37:02.086 --> 00:37:04.020
200,000 kilometers.

00:37:04.088 --> 00:37:06.147
I'm taking the Flyer
into the radiogenic ring.

00:37:06.224 --> 00:37:08.818
With any luck,
they won't follow.

00:37:08.893 --> 00:37:10.485
We can't survive in there
for more than a few minutes.

00:37:10.561 --> 00:37:13.394
That should be enough
to reinitialize the warp core.

00:37:31.115 --> 00:37:33.515
Start continuous transport
of radiogenic particles

00:37:33.584 --> 00:37:35.279
directly into
the reaction chamber.

00:37:35.353 --> 00:37:38.083
When it's approaching
critical mass, let me know.

00:37:38.155 --> 00:37:41.022
Watch for any sign of pursuit.

00:37:41.092 --> 00:37:43.083
How are you doing?

00:37:43.160 --> 00:37:46.596
I always had this alarm
in my head,

00:37:46.664 --> 00:37:50.930
sort of an internal Red Alert.

00:37:51.035 --> 00:37:53.162
It was like a warning system

00:37:53.237 --> 00:37:57.230
that would tell me
I was sick or dying...

00:37:57.308 --> 00:37:58.673
of something.

00:37:58.743 --> 00:38:04.807
Mitochondrial prions,
food poisoning, a head cold.

00:38:04.882 --> 00:38:07.316
It was always there.

00:38:07.385 --> 00:38:09.216
And now it's not?

00:38:11.289 --> 00:38:14.224
It's gone.

00:38:14.292 --> 00:38:16.453
I don't understand.

00:38:16.527 --> 00:38:18.893
Maybe I do.

00:38:19.030 --> 00:38:22.056
When I was a girl,
I was afraid of the ocean.

00:38:22.133 --> 00:38:25.398
I liked to swim, but,
uh, in a pool or a pond,

00:38:25.469 --> 00:38:27.403
where I knew exactly
what was beneath me.

00:38:27.471 --> 00:38:28.733
But in the open water,

00:38:28.806 --> 00:38:31.331
with no way to know
what was down there...

00:38:31.409 --> 00:38:32.876
it scared me to death.

00:38:32.943 --> 00:38:35.878
It wasn't until my first
year at the Academy,

00:38:35.946 --> 00:38:42.408
after I went through zero-G
training in the Coral Sea...

00:38:42.486 --> 00:38:44.954
that I finally got over it.

00:38:47.091 --> 00:38:50.583
I think you just came up
from your first deep dive.

00:38:50.661 --> 00:38:50.761
They're in pursuit.

00:38:50.761 --> 00:38:52.956
They're in pursuit.

00:39:00.037 --> 00:39:01.629
Three minutes,
20 seconds to intercept.

00:39:01.706 --> 00:39:04.436
We'll need twice that
to reinitialize warp reaction.

00:39:04.508 --> 00:39:06.476
Get into the escape pods.

00:39:06.544 --> 00:39:08.136
Captain.

00:39:08.212 --> 00:39:09.975
Plot a course
away from the planet.

00:39:10.047 --> 00:39:11.708
I'm going to fire
a phaser volley

00:39:11.782 --> 00:39:13.716
and hopefully set off
a chain reaction

00:39:13.784 --> 00:39:15.251
of the radiogenic particles.

00:39:15.319 --> 00:39:17.480
It might be enough
to disable our friends.

00:39:17.555 --> 00:39:18.579
You'll be disabled, too.

00:39:18.656 --> 00:39:19.714
Not if I go to full thrusters

00:39:19.790 --> 00:39:21.280
and keep in front
of the shock wave.

00:39:22.860 --> 00:39:24.327
If I don't make it,

00:39:24.395 --> 00:39:25.885
head for the L-Class moon
in the next system.

00:39:25.963 --> 00:39:27.897
You could survive there
for weeks if you have to...

00:39:27.965 --> 00:39:30.900
enough time for Voyager
to pick up your distress signal.

00:39:30.968 --> 00:39:32.162
Now get moving.

00:39:32.236 --> 00:39:33.567
No.

00:39:33.637 --> 00:39:35.730
You'll have a better chance
if we're with you.

00:39:35.806 --> 00:39:36.864
Go.

00:39:36.941 --> 00:39:38.670
We might not have
contributed much

00:39:38.743 --> 00:39:40.904
on Voyager, but what
we do here matters.

00:39:40.978 --> 00:39:41.910
We're the crew here,

00:39:41.979 --> 00:39:45.073
and the crew does not abandon
its captain.

00:39:55.459 --> 00:39:57.427
All right, it's your choice.

00:39:57.495 --> 00:40:00.555
Then I'll be going alone.

00:40:00.631 --> 00:40:03.225
Good luck.

00:40:05.770 --> 00:40:07.499
Charge phaser banks.

00:40:07.571 --> 00:40:11.200
Stand by to divert
all power to thrusters.

00:40:11.275 --> 00:40:14.073
Escape Pod 1 is occupied
and ready, Captain.

00:40:14.145 --> 00:40:16.613
Launch Pod 1.

00:40:16.680 --> 00:40:18.272
Escape pod away.

00:40:18.349 --> 00:40:20.544
How close are our pursuers?

00:40:20.618 --> 00:40:21.744
65 seconds to intercept.

00:40:21.819 --> 00:40:23.047
Stand by to fire.

00:40:24.321 --> 00:40:26.619
Captain, the escape pod
is altering course.

00:40:26.690 --> 00:40:28.214
It's heading for the aliens.

00:40:28.292 --> 00:40:29.919
Janeway to Harren.

00:40:29.994 --> 00:40:30.961
What are you doing?

00:40:31.061 --> 00:40:32.619
If they have to deal with me,

00:40:32.696 --> 00:40:35.426
it should give you
a few more seconds to get away.

00:40:35.499 --> 00:40:36.796
That's my theory, anyway.

00:40:36.867 --> 00:40:39.062
Resume your escape course now.

00:40:39.136 --> 00:40:40.398
It's too late for that.

00:40:40.471 --> 00:40:41.403
You made a mistake,

00:40:41.472 --> 00:40:43.303
Harren. Don't make another one.

00:40:43.374 --> 00:40:44.932
I'm done hiding, Captain.

00:40:45.009 --> 00:40:46.977
A few seconds of exposure
to real life...

00:40:47.111 --> 00:40:51.309
maybe I'll understand
what I've been missing.

00:40:52.383 --> 00:40:53.714
He closed the channel.

00:40:53.784 --> 00:40:54.978
Get a transporter
lock on that pod.

00:40:55.119 --> 00:40:58.384
I-I can't. We're out of range.

00:40:58.456 --> 00:41:00.356
More power to the thrusters.

00:41:06.464 --> 00:41:08.261
Celes.

00:41:08.332 --> 00:41:09.890
We're still not close enough.

00:41:09.967 --> 00:41:11.264
Thrusters at maximum.

00:41:17.308 --> 00:41:17.933
Got him.

00:41:18.075 --> 00:41:19.940
Fire.

00:41:27.518 --> 00:41:28.951
Shock wave approaching.

00:41:29.019 --> 00:41:31.510
Contact in four... three...

00:41:31.589 --> 00:41:34.524
two... one.

00:41:36.427 --> 00:41:38.019
More or less.

00:41:57.414 --> 00:41:58.346
My crew...

00:41:58.415 --> 00:42:00.280
Easy.

00:42:04.555 --> 00:42:05.715
They're sleeping.

00:42:05.789 --> 00:42:07.484
No serious injuries.

00:42:07.558 --> 00:42:09.719
Everyone's all right...

00:42:09.793 --> 00:42:11.454
though you gave us
a good scare for a while.

00:42:12.530 --> 00:42:14.498
We received your distress call.

00:42:14.565 --> 00:42:17.261
We found the Flyer
drifting above a gas giant.

00:42:17.334 --> 00:42:19.495
You were all unconscious.

00:42:19.570 --> 00:42:22.471
Any sign of...

00:42:22.540 --> 00:42:25.407
another vessel or
some kind of entity?

00:42:25.476 --> 00:42:27.273
No.

00:42:30.915 --> 00:42:33.008
What happened?

00:42:34.985 --> 00:42:39.854
The Good Shepherd went
after some lost sheep

00:42:39.924 --> 00:42:44.258
and ran into a wolf.

00:42:44.328 --> 00:42:46.387
Did she find them?

00:42:57.041 --> 00:43:00.374
I think she did.
